# msil-prog.py's usage and configuration errors: exit status 2 and a message
# that names the problem, before any command runs (plan 5.12.4; M14, M20):
# (1) --pipeline obj with --link-output il (obj writes PE images only; M14's
#     errors for --pipeline obj and --link-output pe are gone: both are the
#     defaults from M20), and (2) the equivalence options where they cannot
#     work: --also-il under obj (the text of an LTO link), --equiv-out with
#     --link-output il, --equiv-skip without --test (and the reverse), a
#     malformed --equiv-skip file (an oracle that is none of O3, O4 and O6,
#     whose skip lines the file may hold from M21, and a qualified skip line
#     whose triple is not an MSIL triple), --llc under
#     lto, --llc with a .ll source at -Os, and --equiv-out in native mode;
# (3) a source that does not exist;
# (4) a --workdir that holds a source (the build empties it first);
# (5) bad --archives specifications: no '=', a bad name, a name given twice,
#     an empty source;
# (6) E7 options without all three of --ld-lld, --linux-sysroot and --start
#     (empty ones cancel those of %msil_prog_build under the WSL runner), a
#     sysroot without the E7 libraries, and the E7 recipe for a triple it
#     does not build;
# (7) no --src; (8) a level that does not exist; (9) an empty --ilasm (the
#     il link output needs one); (10) --also-il in native mode.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/w

# (1), (2)
# RUN: %{harness_check} exits 2 %msil_prog_build --pipeline obj --link-output il --level O2 --workdir %t/w --src %t/main.c > %t/1.log 2>&1
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^msil-prog: error: --pipeline obj writes PE images only \(plan 5\.12\.1\); use --link-output pe$"
